Subject: [PATCH 90/95] Reduce allocations and lookups in BlockFlowing

- Slope search (getFlowDirections/slopeDistance) now uses ints and one MutableBlockPosition, and reads each probed position once (the old g() re-read the position it was just handed). Traversal, results and tie handling are unchanged.
- The old EnumSet iterated in EnumDirection ordinal order (NORTH, SOUTH, WEST, EAST); flow is still applied in exactly that order (it decides event order and tick sequence ids), searched in NORTH, EAST, SOUTH, WEST as before.
- Skip the CraftBlock, BlockFromToEvent and dispatch entirely when no plugin listens to BlockFromToEvent (same pattern as the existing no-listener patches).
- canFlowTo is computed from coordinates against the chunk map (what CraftWorld.isChunkLoaded did); allocation change only, loading behavior of the reads is untouched.

Tests: BlockFlowingParityTest compares the new search with a verbatim copy of the old one over >10k randomized positions (water and lava, overworld and nether depths; doors, signs, ladders, reeds, portals, flowing and falling water), pins the NSWE application order and the canFlowTo equivalence. BlockFlowingPerfTest: 20k searches on open terrain, 373 ms -> 217 ms (1.7x), allocation 154 MiB -> 0.5 MiB (~330x). Not covered: full BlockFlowing.b settling (needs a real WorldServer) and the listener-present event path (unchanged code).

